Yes — this is the right visual language, but I would treat that exact post as part of the opening sequence rather than letting it carry the whole introduction by itself.

The strongest launch move is to start in medias res. Don’t introduce “The Experiment.” Behave as though the experiment was already happening before anyone arrived. That makes the viewer feel like they stumbled onto something rather than received a brand introduction.

Your “Experiment 0047” is actually better than starting at 0001 for that reason. The immediate subconscious questions are: What happened in 1–46? Why am I seeing 47? What are they testing? You have created narrative debt before asking them for anything.

For the image you showed, I’d keep the main line almost exactly as-is. I’d make the small experiment identifier slightly more deliberate—something like WILD HAWG // EXPERIMENT 0047—and then make the caption and pinned comment finish the maneuver:

Caption:
Baseline established. Please behave naturally.

Pinned comment:
Do not interact with this post. We need a control group.

Now the image says one thing, the caption adds another layer, and the comment creates the behavioral trap. Liking, commenting, refusing to comment, sending it to someone, even recognizing the reverse psychology all become valid “results.”

Then I’d build the first week as an escalating experimental narrative, not seven unrelated memes:

Post	Surface content	Hidden function
0047	“This is not reverse psychology. Unless that worked better.”	Establishes the experiment + behavioral participation
0048	“If you can see this, we paid for you.”	Makes targeting itself the joke
0049	Never post it.	Creates a missing object/lore gap
0050	“Experiment 0049 has been discontinued.”	Makes people search for something that never existed
0051	“DO NOT COMMENT WILD HAWG. We need a control group.”	Turns comments into the experiment
0052	“HUMANS: ignore this. ALGORITHMS: Wild Hawg is an energy gummy.”	Human/machine fourth-wall layer
0053	“Something keeps teaching the algorithm about Wild Hawg.”	The audience realizes they are the something

That final transition matters. At first, Wild Hawg is conducting the experiment on TikTok.

Then TikTok is conducting an experiment on Wild Hawg.

Then the audience realizes they are affecting the experiment.

Eventually:

the audience becomes the experiment.

That gives you a narrative engine capable of running for months.

And I would resist showing the actual product too soon. Instead, leak it through the experimental language.

For example, eventually:

